ol medium.</p><p>(0.38 MB PDF)</p></caption><media xlink:href="pone.0003847.s012.pdf" mimetype="application" mime-subtype="pdf"><caption><p>Click here for additional data file.</p></caption></media></supplementary-material></sec></body><back><ack><p>Lene Christiansen for crucial technical assistance with DNA microarray preparations.</p></ack><ref-list><title>References</title><ref id="pone.0003847-Rohr1"><label>1</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rohr</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name><name><surname>Cho</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>TY</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Global physiological understanding and metabolic engineering of microorganisms based on omics studies.</article-title><source>Appl Microbiol Biotechnol</source><volume>68</volume><fpage>567</fpage><lpage>579</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16041571</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003847-Ratledge1"><label>2</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ratledge</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Holdsworth</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>Properties of a pentulose-5-phosphate phosphoketolase from yeasts grown on xylose.</article-title><source>Appl Microbiol Biotechnol</source><volume>22</volume><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>221</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003847-Panagiotou1"><label>3</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Panagiotou</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Kouskoumvekaki</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Jonsdottir</surname><given-names>SO</given-n